 ## Background
-Direct Voxel Grid Optimization was introduced by Cheng Sun, Min Sun, and Hwann-Tzong Chen [S1][S5, unofficial]. It addresses the bottleneck of lengthy training times in Neural Radiance Fields (NeRF) [37] by directly optimizing explicit voxel grids. Previous voxel methods often required conversion from trained implicit models or cross-scene pre-training [S1][S5, unofficial]. DVGO demonstrated that direct optimization, combined with post-activation interpolation and specific priors, could achieve NeRF-comparable quality in minutes. It is used on benchmarks such as Syn-NeRF, Syn-NSVF, BlendedMVS, and Tanks and Temples [S1][S5, unofficial].
+Direct Voxel Grid Optimization was introduced by Cheng Sun, Min Sun, and Hwann-Tzong Chen [S1][S5, unofficial]. It addresses the bottleneck of lengthy training times in Neural Radiance Fields (NeRF) [37] by directly optimizing explicit voxel grids [S6]. Previous voxel methods often required conversion from trained implicit models or cross-scene pre-training [S1][S5, unofficial]. DVGO demonstrated that direct optimization, combined with post-activation interpolation and specific priors, could achieve NeRF-comparable quality in minutes [S1]. It is used on benchmarks such as Syn-NeRF, Syn-NSVF, BlendedMVS, and Tanks and Temples [S1][S5, unofficial].
 
